{{- /* dreamteam.alternatives-presentation/v3: fixed text. Both arms get "head" and "foot", the same text byte for byte at one decision point; the treatment adds "comparison" between them and answers inspect with "detail". Every value is a typed field of the view (dreamteam.alternatives-view/v2). */ -}}
{{define "head" -}}
PHASE 3 alternative inspection / PHASE 4 final decision at {{.Time}}. The staffing actions in your reply passed validation: the simulator would accept them now. Nothing has been applied yet.
{{end}}
{{- define "comparison"}}
ALTERNATIVES. The simulator's alternatives to the staffing actions in your reply, in a fixed order: your proposal, no action, then any others the candidate rule lists. The order says nothing about any alternative, and none is a default.
{{- range .Refs}}
{{.ID}} is {{refText .}}.
{{- end}}
{{range .Alternatives}}
{{.ID}}{{if eq .ID "proposal"}} (your proposal){{end}}: {{actions .}}
  Validation: {{validation .}}
{{- end}}

Each alternative's detail gives the simulator's facts and estimates for it, the obligations that continue, its reversibility, and what is not known before deciding. To see details before deciding, reply {"inspect": [ID, ...]}. You can do this once.
{{end}}
{{- define "foot"}}
Reply with one JSON object (the shared system schema governs this phase):
- {"decision": "select", "id": ID, "reason": TEXT} submits the staffing actions of the listed alternative with that ID, unchanged. Your proposal's ID is "proposal".
- {"decision": "revise", "actions": [...], "reason": TEXT} replaces your whole reply with these actions (an empty array is deliberate no action); they are validated again before anything is submitted.
- {"decision": "abandon", "reason": TEXT} submits nothing.
{{- if .Operations}}
Your reply's operations actions ({{.Operations}}) are submitted unchanged with "select"; "revise" replaces them too, and "abandon" submits none of them.
{{- end}}
Optionally add "cite": up to three items from any detail you were shown, each {"item": KEY, "values": {ID: VALUE, ...}}, with the values as shown. The reason is recorded as text.
{{end}}
{{- define "detail" -}}
DETAIL {{.ID}}{{if eq .ID "proposal"}} (your proposal){{end}}: {{actions .}}
  Validation: {{validation .}}
  Facts:
{{- range .Facts}}
    - [{{.Key}}] {{line .}}
{{- else}}
    - none
{{- end}}
  Estimates:
{{- range .Estimates}}
    - [{{.Key}}] {{line .}}
{{- else}}
    - none
{{- end}}
  Obligations that continue:
{{- range .Obligations}}
    - [{{.Key}}] {{line .}}
{{- else}}
    - none listed
{{- end}}
  Continuing employment commitments, relative to no action (each employee once):
{{- range .Commitments}}
    - {{.Ref}} is public staff entry {{.PublicPosition}}. Baseline guarantee: {{cents .BaselineGuarantee}} per full week; continuing guarantee: {{cents .ContinuingGuarantee}} per full week{{if .Through}} through last day {{.Through}}{{end}}; change in weekly rate: {{cents .GuaranteeDelta}}. This is a rate, not a total or future savings.
      Baseline conditional severance exposure: {{cents .BaselineExposure}}; remaining conditional exposure: {{cents .ConditionalExposure}}; change: {{cents .ExposureDelta}}. Exposure is payable only on a later termination, never payable now.{{if .Terminating}} This termination recognizes severance separately in Facts; do not add that recognized amount again as conditional exposure.{{end}}
{{- end}}
  Capacity (whole staffing batch):
    - [slots_closed] Slots closed: {{quantity .Capacity.Closed}}. Capacity, not patients, orders or revenue.
{{- range .Capacity.ClosedByModality}}
      - {{.Modality}}: {{.Count}} slots (same horizon).
{{- end}}
    - [bookings_displaced] Bookings displaced: {{quantity .Capacity.Displaced}}
    - [replacement_capacity] Displaced bookings with feasible replacements by capacity: {{quantity .Capacity.Replacements}}. Acceptance is unavailable before commitment.
    - [slots_opened] Replacement or additional bookable capacity: {{quantity .Capacity.Opened}}
    - Future demand: unavailable. Capacity beyond the displayed horizon: unavailable.
  Withdrawal and reversibility, per action:
{{- range .Reversals}}
